{"seed":{"mim":"615631","entry_type":"phenotype","prefix":"#","title":"ANEMIA, CONGENITAL DYSERYTHROPOIETIC, TYPE Ib","alt_titles":["CDA, TYPE Ib"],"symbol":"CDAN1B","gene_symbols":[],"seed_pmids":[],"max_year":2013},"nodes":[{"id":"entry","type":"Entry","label":"ANEMIA, CONGENITAL DYSERYTHROPOIETIC, TYPE Ib","mim":"615631","entry_type":"phenotype"},{"id":"section:description","type":"Section","label":"description"},{"id":"section:nomenclature","type":"Section","label":"nomenclature"},{"id":"section:cloning_expression","type":"Section","label":"cloning_expression"},{"id":"section:gene_structure","type":"Section","label":"gene_structure"},{"id":"section:clinical_features","type":"Section","label":"clinical_features"},{"id":"section:other_features","type":"Section","label":"other_features"},{"id":"section:biochemical_features","type":"Section","label":"biochemical_features"},{"id":"section:inheritance","type":"Section","label":"inheritance"},{"id":"section:cytogenetics","type":"Section","label":"cytogenetics"},{"id":"section:mapping","type":"Section","label":"mapping"},{"id":"section:heterogeneity","type":"Section","label":"heterogeneity"},{"id":"section:gene_function","type":"Section","label":"gene_function"},{"id":"section:molecular_genetics","type":"Section","label":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"section:genotype_phenotype_correlations","type":"Section","label":"genotype_phenotype_correlations"},{"id":"section:pathogenesis","type":"Section","label":"pathogenesis"},{"id":"section:diagnosis","type":"Section","label":"diagnosis"},{"id":"section:clinical_management","type":"Section","label":"clinical_management"},{"id":"section:population_genetics","type":"Section","label":"population_genetics"},{"id":"section:evolution","type":"Section","label":"evolution"},{"id":"section:animal_model","type":"Section","label":"animal_model"},{"id":"section:history","type":"Section","label":"history"},{"id":"paper:23716552","type":"Paper","label":"Babbs et al. (2013)","pmid":"23716552","year":2013,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Homozygous mutations in a predicted endonuclease are a novel cause of congenital dyserythropoietic anemia type I."},{"id":"paper:16754775","type":"Paper","label":"Ahmed et al. (2006)","pmid":"16754775","year":2006,"content_level":"title","relevance":"supporting","title":"Linkage and mutational analysis of the CDAN1 gene reveals genetic heterogeneity in congenital dyserythropoietic anemia type I."},{"id":"paper:16643456","type":"Paper","label":"Ahmed et al. (2006)","pmid":"16643456","year":2006,"content_level":"title","relevance":"supporting","title":"Evidence of genetic heterogeneity in congenital dyserythropoietic anaemia type I."},{"id":"paper:9220189","type":"Paper","label":"Sabry et al. (1997)","pmid":"9220189","year":1997,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Non-haematological traits associated with congenital dyserythropoietic anaemia type 1: a new entity emerging."},{"id":"finding:9220189:1","type":"Finding","label":"Sabry et al. (1997) described 3 Bedouin sibs with congenital dyserythropoietic anemia type I who also had dysmorphic features. These included growth retardation/short stature, congenital ptosis, abnormal tarsal bones, metatarsal duplication/hypoplasia, nail and phalangeal hypoplasia of fingers and toes, Madelung deformity, syndactyly of toes, and hallux valgus. The phenotype varied among the sibs.","pmid":"9220189","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0004810","type":"Phenotype","label":"Congenital hypoplastic anemia","hpo_id":"HP:0004810"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0004322","type":"Phenotype","label":"Short stature","hpo_id":"HP:0004322"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000508","type":"Phenotype","label":"Ptosis","hpo_id":"HP:0000508"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001850","type":"Phenotype","label":"Abnormality of the tarsal bones","hpo_id":"HP:0001850"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001832","type":"Phenotype","label":"Abnormal metatarsal morphology","hpo_id":"HP:0001832"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0002164","type":"Phenotype","label":"Nail dysplasia","hpo_id":"HP:0002164"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0009803","type":"Phenotype","label":"Short phalanx of finger","hpo_id":"HP:0009803"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0003067","type":"Phenotype","label":"Madelung deformity","hpo_id":"HP:0003067"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001770","type":"Phenotype","label":"Toe syndactyly","hpo_id":"HP:0001770"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001822","type":"Phenotype","label":"Hallux valgus","hpo_id":"HP:0001822"},{"id":"finding:9220189:2","type":"Finding","label":"Sabry et al. (1997) found a very low mitotic index in peripheral blood lymphocyte cultures from the 3 affected sibs. They suggested that a low mitotic index and congenital ptosis could be part of the syndrome.","pmid":"9220189","section":"biochemical_features"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0004332","type":"Phenotype","label":"Abnormal lymphocyte morphology","hpo_id":"HP:0004332"},{"id":"finding:9220189:3","type":"Finding","label":"Sabry et al. (1997) concluded that their report confirmed an association between a subset of congenital dyserythropoietic anemia type I and a specific form of distal limb anomalies. This suggested a distinct entity.","pmid":"9220189","section":"heterogeneity"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0040064","type":"Phenotype","label":"Abnormality of limbs","hpo_id":"HP:0040064"},{"id":"finding:16643456:1","type":"Finding","label":"Ahmed et al. (2006) reported evidence of genetic heterogeneity in congenital dyserythropoietic anemia type I.","pmid":"16643456","section":"heterogeneity"},{"id":"finding:16754775:1","type":"Finding","label":"Ahmed et al. (2006) performed linkage and mutation analysis of the CDAN1 gene in congenital dyserythropoietic anemia type I and found genetic heterogeneity.","pmid":"16754775","section":"heterogeneity"},{"id":"gene:CDAN1","type":"Gene","label":"CDAN1"},{"id":"finding:23716552:1","type":"Finding","label":"In a consanguineous family of Middle Eastern origin with congenital dyserythropoietic anemia type I, Babbs et al. (2013) used whole genome sequencing and segregation analysis to identify a homozygous c.533T>A transversion in the C15ORF41 gene, which was predicted to result in a p.L178Q substitution. No likely pathogenic CDAN1 mutation had been found in this family.","pmid":"23716552","section":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"gene:CDIN1","type":"Gene","label":"CDIN1"},{"id":"variant:CDIN1:c.533T>A","type":"Variant","label":"CDIN1 c.533T>A / p.L178Q","gene":"CDIN1","keys":["c.533T>A","p.L178Q"],"omim_name":"CDIN1, LEU178GLN"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0005532","type":"Phenotype","label":"Macrocytic dyserythropoietic anemia","hpo_id":"HP:0005532"},{"id":"inh:AR","type":"Inheritance","label":"Autosomal recessive","hpo_id":"HP:0000007"},{"id":"finding:23716552:2","type":"Finding","label":"By sequencing C15ORF41 in other congenital dyserythropoietic anemia type I families without CDAN1 mutations, Babbs et al. (2013) found a homozygous c.281A>G transition, predicted to result in a p.Y94C substitution, in 2 more families of Southeast Asian origin.","pmid":"23716552","section":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"variant:CDIN1:c.281A>G","type":"Variant","label":"CDIN1 c.281A>G / p.Y94C","gene":"CDIN1","keys":["c.281A>G","p.Y94C"],"omim_name":"CDIN1, TYR94CYS"},{"id":"finding:23716552:3","type":"Finding","label":"Babbs et al. (2013) reported that the haplotype around the c.281A>G mutation in C15ORF41 suggested a founder effect for this mutation in Pakistan.","pmid":"23716552","section":"population_genetics"},{"id":"finding:23716552:4","type":"Finding","label":"Babbs et al. (2013) noted that CDAN1 mutations underlie most cases of congenital dyserythropoietic anemia type I. However, no likely pathogenic CDAN1 mutation is found in about 20% of cases, which suggested that at least one other locus exists.","pmid":"23716552","section":"heterogeneity"},{"id":"finding:23716552:5","type":"Finding","label":"Using detailed sequence similarity searches, Babbs et al. (2013) predicted that C15ORF41 encodes a novel restriction endonuclease belonging to the Holliday junction resolvase protein family.","pmid":"23716552","section":"pathogenesis"}],"edges":[{"src":"paper:9220189","rel":"reports","dst":"finding:9220189:1"},{"src":"finding:9220189:1","rel":"in_section","dst":"section:clinical_features"},{"src":"finding:9220189:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0004810","pmid":"9220189","present":true,"frequency":"3/3","text":"congenital dyserythropoietic anemia type 1"},{"src":"finding:9220189:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0004322","pmid":"9220189","present":true,"text":"growth retardation/short stature"},{"src":"finding:9220189:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0000508","pmid":"9220189","present":true,"text":"congenital ptosis"},{"src":"finding:9220189:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0001850","pmid":"9220189","present":true,"text":"abnormal tarsal bones"},{"src":"finding:9220189:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0001832","pmid":"9220189","present":true,"text":"metatarsal duplication/hypoplasia"},{"src":"finding:9220189:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0002164","pmid":"9220189","present":true,"text":"nail hypoplasia of fingers and toes"},{"src":"finding:9220189:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0009803","pmid":"9220189","present":true,"text":"phalangeal hypoplasia"},{"src":"finding:9220189:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0003067","pmid":"9220189","present":true,"text":"Madelung deformity"},{"src":"finding:9220189:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0001770","pmid":"9220189","present":true,"text":"syndactyly of toes"},{"src":"finding:9220189:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0001822","pmid":"9220189","present":true,"text":"hallux valgus"},{"src":"paper:9220189","rel":"reports","dst":"finding:9220189:2"},{"src":"finding:9220189:2","rel":"in_section","dst":"section:biochemical_features"},{"src":"finding:9220189:2","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0004332","pmid":"9220189","present":true,"frequency":"3/3","text":"very low mitotic index of peripheral blood lymphocyte cultures"},{"src":"paper:922